, rear lap seam, two reinforcement plates, two pivot pins, two terminal eyes, formed bail and bored wooden grip.","mounting":"Heel annulus bears on y=0. Pin radius 2.5 mm inside terminal-eye bore 2.8 mm; nominal radial clearance 0.3 mm.","interfaces":"Floor crimp intentionally joins lower wall; plate backs follow wall taper with local welded overlap. Pin radius 2.5 mm inside terminal bore 2.8 mm. Wood bore radius 3 mm around 2.5 mm wire; straight bridge through grip. Full assembly interference review remains pending.","orientation":"Upright; inside sheltered relative to outside; no water or contents.","aging":"Intact dry zinc and dry wood. Fine coating variation only; no arbitrary rust/scratches or falsely painted specular spots.","geometryVsMaterial":"Thin shell, curled lip, heel crimp, seam, eyes, pins, bail and grip bore modeled. Coating microstructure in albedo/roughness, normal scale zero.","period":"Manufacturer demonstrates galvanized buckets and crimp construction; source is modern and NOT evidence of this exact configuration in 1990s.","references":["https://shop.onoess.co.jp/ja-jp/products/4907797001066","https://www.onoess.co.jp/"],"lod":"All 11 components retained at every LOD. Reduction changes angular sampling only, not physical part presence."},"verification":{"unityCompile":false,"unityImport":false,"unityRender":false,"visualFidelity":"UNSCORED_UNTIL_REAL_4K_RENDER","visualPointsAwarded":0}}
